target: internal/report/post.go
verify: go test ./internal/report/ -count=1 -run 'TestTheBranchesNothingReached/a_budget_that_expires'
expect: --- FAIL:
why:    with NO deadline arm at all, a budget that expires in the LookPath-plus-fork window answers "gh could not be run … install gh or post the report by hand" for a gh the caller's own deadline cancelled — the one remedy that cannot help, and the advice the default arm's comment says must never be given for a killed gh. `Start` checks the context after LookPath and returns ctx.Err(), which is not an *exec.ExitError and names no process, so it falls to the never-started test below. Measured: budget 1ns gives `context deadline exceeded` (a context.deadlineExceededError), budget 1ms gives `signal: killed` (an ExitError the default arm already handles) — the two halves of one cause arriving on opposite sides of the test. This entry removes the arm; report-cancelled-probe-asks-the-clock guards the weaker form, where the arm is present but tests the clock instead of the error. `case false:` rather than a deletion only so the arm's body stays attached to a case; `ctx`, `errors` and `context` are all still referenced by the rest of the function either way.
--- old
	case errors.Is(err, context.DeadlineExceeded), errors.Is(err, context.Canceled):
--- new
	case false:
